[38;5;252m[1m## Behavioral verification[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I built a differential harness that [38;5;10mdlopen[0ms both libraries and compares [1mraw bit patterns[22m of every return value and every out-parameter. All 38 symbols are exercised (I verified the harness generates exactly 38 binding sites). Coverage includes randomized and edge-case floats, subnormals, degenerate geometry (point AABBs, inverted AABBs, zero-length capsules, zero radii), all 16 [38;5;10mc2Collided[0m type pairs including invalid enum values, [38;5;10mc2Simplex[0m counts 0–4 to hit every [38;5;10mdefault:[0m branch, NULL out-params, and GJK cache cold/warm/reused paths.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m4,128,288 checks, 0 failures[22m — against the C compiled at [38;5;10m-O0[0m, [38;5;10m-O1[0m, [38;5;10m-O2[0m, [38;5;10m-O3[0m, and the default CMake build.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## One finding worth reporting[0m[0m
[0m[0m
With Inf/NaN inputs, a few thousand float results differ in the NaN sign bit ([38;5;10m0x7fc00000[0m vs [38;5;10m0xffc00000[0m). This is [38;5;10maddss[0m operand-order selection when [3mboth[23m addends are NaN — the hardware returns whichever operand the compiler placed in the destination register.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This is not a translation defect: the C does not agree with itself here. Compiled at [38;5;10m-O0[0m versus [38;5;10m-O3[0m, the same C source produces [1m2010 mismatches[22m on the same inputs, affecting the same functions at comparable magnitude to Rust-vs-C. [38;5;10mc2Dot[0m flips between [38;5;10m-O0[0m and [38;5;10m-O1[0m; [38;5;10mc2Add[0m flips between [38;5;10m-O2[0m and [38;5;10m-O3[0m. I deliberately did not hard-code per-expression NaN choices, since that would overfit to one GCC version and flag combination and would be wrong for others. Every integer-returning function — [38;5;10maabb[0m, [38;5;10mc2Collided[0m, [38;5;10mc2Support[0m, and all six boolean predicates — is bit-identical at every optimization level in every mode, including with Inf/NaN.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Fidelity notes[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Bugs and quirks were reproduced rather than fixed: the inverted cache-validity test in [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m ([38;5;10mmetric < -1.0e8f[0m), [38;5;10mc2Support[0m reading [38;5;10mverts[0][0m unconditionally even when [38;5;10mcount <= 0[0m, the [38;5;10mdefault:[0m/[38;5;10mcase 1:[0m fall-through in [38;5;10mc2GJKSimplexMetric[0m, ternary min/max instead of [38;5;10mfminf[0m/[38;5;10mfmaxf[0m (which differ on NaN), and [38;5;10mc2MakeProxy[0m leaving the proxy untouched for an unknown type. [38;5;10mc2Simplex[0m models the C's [38;5;10mc2sv a,b,c,d[0m as [38;5;10m[c2sv; 4][0m because the C walks them as an array via [38;5;10mc2sv *verts = &s.a;[0m — [38;5;10mc2sv[0m is 36 bytes with alignment 4, so the layout matches exactly. The by-value struct ABI, including the 20-byte [38;5;10mc2Capsule[0m that classifies as MEMORY and the 16-byte [38;5;10mc2x[0m passed in two SSE registers, is confirmed correct by the passing tests.[0m[0m
