The one intentional deviation: [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m's local [38;5;10mc2Proxy[0m objects are uninitialized in C, so an invalid [38;5;10mC2_TYPE[0m makes it read indeterminate stack bytes. I zero-initialize instead, which is deterministic. This is unreachable through any valid input, and it was in fact what my first harness draft accidentally probed — the apparent GJK failures vanished once I constrained cache indices to each proxy's actual vertex count.[0m[0m
